            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic possibilities and limitations of the necropsy examination on cadavers exhumed because of sudden cardiac death].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After presenting five individual cases, the authors confirm the possibility of a diagnosis of sudden cardiac death where myocardial and/or coronary arteries lesions were present, by performing an exhumed body's autopsy even after a considerable amount of time after death. With regard to this procedure, performed only by experienced consultants specializing, a particularly accurate verification is necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
